  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-107738",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the volume of the bar of chocolate.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9,\\,w=5,\\,h=2\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=9\\cdot 5\\cdot 2=90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe total volume of the four bars of chocolate is\n\n$$\n90\\cdot 4=360\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the cost of four chocolate bars is\n\n$$\n360\\cdot 0.02=$7.20.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
